---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Best practices">
  <p>
    These habits get you better matches from the API and a smoother
    experience for your users.
  </p>

  <h2>Always include duration</h2>
  <p>
    The <code>duration</code> parameter makes a big difference to matching.
    It helps tell apart:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Radio edits vs album versions</li>
    <li>Live vs studio recordings</li>
    <li>Different songs with similar names</li>
  </ul>
  <pre><code class="language-bash">{`# Good - includes duration
/getLyrics?s=Bohemian%20Rhapsody&a=Queen&al=A%20Night%20at%20the%20Opera&d=354

# Less accurate - missing duration
/getLyrics?s=Bohemian%20Rhapsody&a=Queen&al=A%20Night%20at%20the%20Opera`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    Always include it, together with the album. The cache key includes both, so a request
    without them often misses the cached entry and, without an API key, returns <code>401</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Always include the album name</h2>
  <p>
    Including the album name helps the API find the correct version of a song,
    especially when:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>The song appears on multiple albums</li>
    <li>There are remastered or deluxe editions</li>
    <li>The artist has re-recorded songs</li>
  </ul>
  <pre><code class="language-bash">{`# Recommended - includes album
/getLyrics?s=Yesterday&a=The%20Beatles&al=Help!&d=125

# Less specific - may return wrong version
/getLyrics?s=Yesterday&a=The%20Beatles&d=125`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    The API accepts a request without an album, but the cache key includes it, so a request without
    it often misses the cached entry and, without an API key, returns <code>401</code>. Always send it.
  </p>

  <h2>Trim whitespace from input</h2>
  <p>
    The API normalizes input on the server, but trimming leading and trailing
    whitespace before you send can still improve cache hit rates:
  </p>
  <pre><code class="language-javascript">{`// Before
song = "  E85  "

// After
song = song.trim() // "E85"`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Implement client-side caching</h2>
  <p>
    Reduce API calls by caching responses locally:
  </p>
  <pre><code class="language-javascript">{`const lyricsCache = new Map();

async function getLyrics(song, artist, album, duration) {
  const key = \`\${song.toLowerCase()}|\${artist.toLowerCase()}|\${album.toLowerCase()}|\${duration}\`;

  if (lyricsCache.has(key)) {
    return lyricsCache.get(key);
  }

  const result = await fetchFromAPI(song, artist, album, duration);
  lyricsCache.set(key, result);

  return result;
}`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    To keep it across sessions, persist the cache to localStorage or IndexedDB.
  </p>

  <h2>Handle negative cache hits</h2>
  <p>
    When you receive <code>X-Cache-Status: NEGATIVE_HIT</code>, the API previously
    searched for this song and found no lyrics. Don't retry immediately.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Store negative results locally to avoid repeat requests</li>
    <li>Show a "lyrics not available" message to users</li>
    <li>If you know lyrics should exist, use <code>/revalidate</code> (requires API key)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Respect rate limits</h2>
  <p>
    For production applications:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Play uncached songs through the <a href="https://better-lyrics.boidu.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Better Lyrics</a> extension first to populate the cache</li>
    <li>Queue requests to avoid bursts</li>
    <li>Add delays between batch requests</li>
    <li>Back off when you get a 429</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Pre-fetch upcoming songs</h2>
  <p>
    If you know which songs play next, fetch their lyrics early:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Fetch lyrics when a playlist loads, not when each song starts</li>
    <li>Limit concurrent requests to avoid rate limiting</li>
    <li>Prioritize songs near the current playback position</li>
  </ul>
  <pre><code class="language-javascript">{`// Pre-fetch next 3 songs in playlist
async function prefetchPlaylist(playlist, currentIndex) {
  const toFetch = playlist.slice(currentIndex, currentIndex + 3);

  for (const track of toFetch) {
    // Stagger requests to avoid bursts
    await fetchLyrics(track.song, track.artist, track.album, track.duration);
    await sleep(200);
  }
}`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Parse TTML efficiently</h2>
  <p>
    TTML parsing can be expensive. A few ways to keep it cheap:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Parse once and cache the structured result</li>
    <li>Use a Web Worker for parsing if it blocks the main thread</li>
    <li>Pre-compute the next few lines during playback</li>
    <li>Use <a href="/braccato/parsers"><code>@braccato/parsers</code></a> (built from the Better Lyrics parsers) instead of writing your own</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Handle missing timing</h2>
  <p>
    Timing data can be incomplete in some documents:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Check that <code>begin</code> and <code>end</code> attributes exist</li>
    <li>Validate that times are parseable</li>
    <li>Fall back to line-level display if syllable timing is missing</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Test with edge cases</h2>
  <p>
    Test your integration with:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Songs with special characters in names</li>
    <li>Very long songs (10+ minutes)</li>
    <li>RTL languages (Arabic, Hebrew)</li>
    <li>Songs with no lyrics available</li>
    <li>Songs with instrumental sections</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Monitor your usage</h2>
  <p>
    Track these to see how your integration behaves:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Cache hit rate (from <code>X-Cache-Status</code> header)</li>
    <li>Error rate by status code</li>
    <li>Response times</li>
    <li>Rate limit encounters</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Attribute Better Lyrics</h2>
  <p>
    If your project uses this API, consider adding a link to
    <a href="https://better-lyrics.boidu.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Better Lyrics</a>
    in your app or README. It helps other people find the project and keeps development going.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
